  "query_preview": "..\n\nA couple of changes to the long term forecast going forward, but\nstill within the same flavor as yesterday's forecast. Tuesday\nlooks increasingly like a less rainy day. With the cold air\nadvection building surface high pressure in the central gulf,\nprecipitation chances have been reduced down to just a chance for\nthe Icy Strait corridor, and almost removed entirely for the \nsouthern half of the panhandle. Could also see some clearing in \nthe southern half of the panhandle as well from the ample dry air \naloft. Going into Wednesday, this ridge over the gulf quickly \nbreaks down, as rain chances increase again. Still expecting to \nsee mostly ridging for the southern panhandle, directing a \nmajority of the moisture towards the NE gulf coast and Icy Strait \ncorridor. This trend looks looks to continue towards the end of \nthe week, with a general active and wet pattern.",
